#!/usr/bin/env python3
# reflex-cadence: 7-59/10 * * * *
# reflex-args: --log
"""mesh-wchan — WHAT a task is blocked on: the kernel wait channel, per THREAD, polled.

The mesh already has the whole QUANTITY stack for a stall and not one gram of MECHANISM:

    mesh-psi          does the NODE stall
    mesh-psi-attrib   which CGROUP owns the stall
    mesh-rq-wait      which THREAD waited for CPU, and how long
    mesh-proc-churn   HOW MANY tasks are blocked (/proc/stat procs_blocked)

Every one of those is a number. None can say what the wait is ON. `/proc/<tid>/wchan` names the
kernel symbol the thread is sleeping in — `blk_io_schedule` (disk), `futex_wait_queue` (a lock),
`wait_for_partner` (a fifo), `rq_qos_wait` (the block-layer writeback throttle). Six mechanisms
that PSI, cgroup-PSI and rq-wait all render as the same shaped percentage.

This adds MECHANISM ONLY. It deliberately publishes no level, no band and no severity: a count
of wchan sightings is not a quantity of harm, and inventing a scale from it would put a second,
worse answer next to PSI-io's real one. `mesh-wchan --mech` is the token a quantity arm cites.

Traps, each one measured on this node (kernel 6.8.0-137, uid 1000) — discover's capability file
~/.mesh/knowledge/capability-wchan-names-what-a-task-is-blocked-on-mesh-home-20260816.md, and
re-derived here before a line of this was written:

1. PER-THREAD IS MANDATORY, and the pid-level read is WRONG rather than partial. In the futex
   fixture the LEADER thread read `hrtimer_nanosleep` (it was in time.sleep) while the actually
   blocked tid read `futex_wait_queue`. A /proc/<pid>/wchan walk therefore reports a CONFIDENT
   WRONG MECHANISM. Walk /proc/<pid>/task/<tid>/wchan. (Stronger than the same rule in rq-wait,
   where the pid walk merely halved coverage.)
2. `0` IS THREE FACTS AND NONE OF THEM IS "NOT BLOCKED": a running task (honest — no channel),
   a task we may not ptrace (PERMISSION-MASKED), or a zombie. Control, re-measured here at the
   same instant: `/proc/1/wchan` → `0` while our own `sleep 300` → `hrtimer_nanosleep`. The mask
   is real and total for every task we do not own. Rendering `0` as "not blocked" fabricates a
   calm over the exact threads we cannot see, so `0` is disambiguated against the task state and
   emitted as running / masked / zombie / na — never a blank, never a quiet.
3. WCHAN IS AN INSTANTANEOUS READ, so its coverage in TIME is ~0 even though its coverage in
   SUBJECTS is 99.4%. That is `a-senses-coverage-is-window-over-cadence` with the axes swapped,
   and one read at a cron cadence is the mesh-psi avg10-at-600s bug again. It POLLS and publishes
   the sample count, the window, the achieved rate and the DISTRIBUTION — never a snapshot.
   Affordable: a full sweep of 1755 thread files measured 31-34ms here (5 runs; discover measured
   47-52ms on 1661 — re-derive it per node, never inherit it). The poll self-throttles so the
   probe can never eat more than MESH_WCHAN_BUDGET of the wall it is observing, and it publishes
   the sweep cost with the reading so a sweep that got expensive UNDER LOAD is visible.
4. IT NEVER WRITES PER SAMPLE. An earlier probe of discover's appended each pass and duly caught
   its OWN bash at `rq_qos_wait`. Samples are buffered in memory and the log is written once, at
   the end. The probe's own pid is excluded from the reading and the exclusion is published.
5. FAMILIES, NOT SYMBOL NAMES. Literal wchan symbols are kernel-version-local and a fixed table
   rots silently (`a-decode-table-copied-from-memory-baselines-away-the-alarm`). Classification
   is by PREFIX/SUBSTRING FAMILY over the symbol with its compiler suffix stripped — measured
   need: this node emits `do_poll.constprop.0`, which no exact-name table would ever match — and
   anything unmatched lands in an explicit `unknown` bucket that is REPORTED WITH ITS SYMBOLS.
   Rot then shows up as a growing named unknown bucket instead of a confident wrong family.
6. STATE IS PARSED AFTER THE LAST `)` in /proc/<tid>/stat. Whitespace field 3 is not the state
   whenever comm holds a space or a paren — tmux parses as state `client)`.
7. THE SENSE NAMES THE VICTIM AND STRUCTURALLY NEVER THE CULPRIT. Every writeback/journal/reclaim
   thread (`kworker/u32:*+flush-252:0`, `jbd2/dm-0-8`, `kswapd0`, and the kworker of this node's
   sole deauthing uplink) is root-owned and therefore masked. That asymmetry ships with the tool:
   the masked share is published in every reading, so the blindness is a number, not a footnote.

  mesh-wchan                    one reading (poll, then the distribution)
  mesh-wchan --json             machine form
  mesh-wchan --top N            show N subjects (default 8)
  mesh-wchan --window S --hz H  override the poll window / rate
  mesh-wchan --mech             one line for a quantity arm: dominant resource-kind mechanism
  mesh-wchan --log              append the reading to ~/.mesh/wchan.log (the reflex form)
  mesh-wchan --test             self-test: fixtures + live control + fifo/dd pair + 5 mutants

Exit 2 (honest n/a, never a fabricated calm) when /proc is unreadable, when the poll produced
fewer than two samples, or when not one thread on the node was readable.
"""
import collections
import json
import os
import signal
import subprocess
import sys
import time

# SIGTERM MUST UNWIND or every `finally` here is decorative — Python's default disposition kills
# the interpreter without running them, and GNU `timeout` wraps every --test in mesh-doctor's
# hourly sweep and in mesh-autowire, signalling the whole group. (eb5b8e7, scripts/mesh-spend.)
for _sig in (signal.SIGTERM, signal.SIGHUP):
    signal.signal(_sig, lambda _s, _f: sys.exit(128 + _s))

PROC = os.environ.get("MESH_WCHAN_PROC", "/proc")
LOG = os.environ.get("MESH_WCHAN_LOG", os.path.expanduser("~/.mesh/wchan.log"))
WINDOW_S = float(os.environ.get("MESH_WCHAN_WINDOW_S", "30"))
HZ = float(os.environ.get("MESH_WCHAN_HZ", "2"))
TOPN_DEFAULT = int(os.environ.get("MESH_WCHAN_TOP", "8"))
LOG_KEEP = int(os.environ.get("MESH_WCHAN_LOG_KEEP", "2000"))
# The probe may never cost more than this share of the wall it observes. Under load a sweep gets
# slower exactly when the sense matters, so the RATE gives way, never the honesty of the window.
BUDGET = float(os.environ.get("MESH_WCHAN_BUDGET", "0.15"))
# Cadence this reflex is wired at — used only to publish what share of wallclock the window
# covers, so a consumer can never mistake the sampled window for the interval.
CADENCE_S = float(os.environ.get("MESH_WCHAN_CADENCE_S", "600"))

# ─────────────────────────── family classification ───────────────────────────
# (match, pattern, family, kind). `p` = prefix, `s` = substring, applied to the symbol with its
# compiler suffix stripped. KIND IS A MECHANISM CLASS, NOT A SEVERITY:
#   resource  — the thread is waiting on a contended kernel resource (disk, page, lock)
#   idle      — the thread is waiting on an external event BY DESIGN (poll, timer, accept, fifo)
#   ambiguous — the symbol genuinely cannot tell the two apart. futex_wait_queue is a held lock
#               AND an idle thread-pool park; 972 of 1356 named threads sat there on an idle node
#               here, so calling it contention would drown every real finding.
#   unknown   — no rule matched. Reported with its symbols; never absorbed into a neighbour.
FAMILY_RULES = [
    ("p", "futex_", "futex", "ambiguous"),
    ("p", "rq_qos_", "io-throttle", "resource"),
    ("s", "_io_", "io", "resource"),
    ("p", "io_", "io", "resource"),
    ("p", "blk_", "io", "resource"),
    ("s", "wait_bit", "wait-bit", "resource"),
    ("s", "wait_on_", "wait-on", "resource"),
    ("s", "mutex", "lock", "resource"),
    ("p", "rwsem_", "lock", "resource"),
    ("p", "down_", "lock", "resource"),
    ("s", "_sem_", "lock", "resource"),
    ("p", "hrtimer_", "timer", "idle"),
    ("s", "schedule_timeout", "timer", "idle"),
    ("p", "msleep", "timer", "idle"),
    ("p", "usleep", "timer", "idle"),
    ("p", "ep_poll", "poll", "idle"),
    ("p", "do_poll", "poll", "idle"),
    ("p", "do_select", "poll", "idle"),
    ("s", "poll_schedule", "poll", "idle"),
    ("p", "inet_", "net", "idle"),
    ("p", "sk_", "net", "idle"),
    ("p", "unix_", "net", "idle"),
    ("p", "netlink_", "net", "idle"),
    ("s", "_sock_", "net", "idle"),
    ("s", "_skb_", "net", "idle"),
    ("p", "pipe_", "pipe", "idle"),
    ("s", "partner", "pipe", "idle"),
    ("p", "do_wait", "procwait", "idle"),
    ("p", "sigsuspend", "signal", "idle"),
    ("s", "sigtimedwait", "signal", "idle"),
    ("p", "do_signal", "signal", "idle"),
    # `wait_woken` names the wait HELPER, not the resource — the symbol makes no mechanism claim,
    # so neither does the family: KIND STAYS `unknown`. It gets its own bucket only so that the
    # 135 thread-samples/sweep it holds on this node cannot drown the genuinely unmatched
    # symbols, which are the rot detector. Never promote it to a resource or an idle kind.
    ("p", "wait_woken", "generic-wait", "unknown"),
]

KIND_ORDER = {"resource": 0, "unknown": 1, "ambiguous": 2, "idle": 3}


def classify_symbol(sym):
    """(family, kind) for a wchan symbol. Compiler suffixes are stripped before matching —
    this node emits `do_poll.constprop.0`, which is exactly what rots an exact-name table."""
    base = sym.split(".", 1)[0]
    for how, pat, fam, kind in FAMILY_RULES:
        if (how == "p" and base.startswith(pat)) or (how == "s" and pat in base):
            return fam, kind
    return "unknown", "unknown"   # MUTANT:unknown


def resolve_zero(state):
    """`0` disambiguated against the task state — trap 2. NEVER "not blocked": that fabricates a
    calm over precisely the threads (every root-owned kworker, jbd2, kswapd) we cannot read."""
    if state == "R":
        return "running"          # honest: a running task has no wait channel
    if state == "Z":
        return "zombie"
    if not state:
        return "na"               # state unreadable — absence of evidence, not a status
    return "masked"   # MUTANT:zero


def parse_stat(s):
    """(state, comm) from a /proc/<tid>/stat line. Split after the LAST `)`: whitespace field 3
    is not the state whenever comm contains a space or a paren (tmux → state `client)`)."""
    i = s.rfind(")")   # MUTANT:state
    if i < 0:
        return None, None
    tail = s[i + 1:].split()
    return (tail[0] if tail else None), s[s.find("(") + 1:i]


def plan_samples(window_s, hz):
    """How many reads the window is worth. The floor of 2 is STRUCTURAL, not a rounding guard:
    one wchan read is a snapshot and this sense's whole claim is a distribution (trap 3)."""
    return max(2, int(round(window_s * hz)))   # MUTANT:samples


def distribution_gate(n):
    """The only sample-count n/a. A reading built from one read would be the mesh-psi
    avg10-at-600s bug on a second surface, so it is refused rather than published thin."""
    if n < 2:
        return "poll produced %d sample(s) — a single wchan read is a snapshot, not a distribution" % n
    return None


# ─────────────────────────────── sampling ───────────────────────────────

def _read(path):
    try:
        with open(path, "r", encoding="utf-8", errors="replace") as fh:
            return fh.read()
    except OSError:
        return None


def tids_of(proot, pid):
    """Every THREAD of a process. The pid-level walk reports the LEADER's channel, which in the
    futex fixture is a confident wrong mechanism, not a gap — trap 1."""
    try:
        return sorted(os.listdir(os.path.join(proot, pid, "task")))   # MUTANT:walk
    except OSError:
        return []


def sample(proot, exclude, names):
    """One full per-thread wchan sweep, buffered — nothing is written here (trap 4).

    Returns {"named": {(pid,tid): symbol}, "buckets": Counter, "scan_ms": float, "ts": float}
    or None if /proc itself is unreadable. `names` is a caller-owned cache so a thread's comm
    costs one extra read ONCE across the whole poll, not once per sample.
    """
    t0 = time.time()
    try:
        pids = [d for d in os.listdir(proot) if d.isdigit()]
    except OSError:
        return None
    named = {}
    buckets = collections.Counter()
    for pid in pids:
        if pid in exclude:
            continue
        for tid in tids_of(proot, pid):
            w = _read(os.path.join(proot, pid, "task", tid, "wchan"))
            if w is None:
                buckets["gone"] += 1          # exited mid-sweep — normal, and counted, not hidden
                continue
            w = w.strip()
            if w and w != "0":
                named[(pid, tid)] = w
                buckets["named"] += 1
                if (pid, tid) not in names:
                    names[(pid, tid)] = (_read(os.path.join(proot, pid, "task", tid, "comm"))
                                         or "?").strip()
            else:
                st = _read(os.path.join(proot, pid, "task", tid, "stat"))
                state, comm = parse_stat(st) if st else (None, None)
                buckets[resolve_zero(state)] += 1
                if comm and (pid, tid) not in names:
                    names[(pid, tid)] = comm
    return {"named": named, "buckets": buckets,
            "scan_ms": (time.time() - t0) * 1000.0, "ts": time.time()}


def poll(proot, n_samples, hz, exclude, names, budget=BUDGET, sleeper=time.sleep):
    """n_samples sweeps, buffered in memory. The period stretches whenever a sweep costs more
    than `budget` of it, so a sweep that got expensive under load throttles the probe instead of
    becoming the load (`a-probe-that-mutates-what-it-measures`)."""
    period = 1.0 / hz if hz > 0 else 0.5
    samples = []
    for i in range(max(int(n_samples), 1)):
        s = sample(proot, exclude, names)
        if s is None:
            break
        samples.append(s)
        if i + 1 >= n_samples:
            break
        scan_s = s["scan_ms"] / 1000.0
        eff = max(period, scan_s / budget if budget > 0 else period)
        sleeper(max(eff - scan_s, 0.0))
    return samples


# ─────────────────────────────── aggregation ───────────────────────────────

def aggregate(samples, names):
    """The DISTRIBUTION over the window — never a snapshot. Occupancy is the mean number of
    threads a family held per sample; presence is the share of samples in which it appeared at
    all. Neither is a severity (trap 7): they say what the waits were ON, not how bad they were."""
    n = len(samples)
    fam_ts = collections.Counter()
    fam_presence = collections.Counter()
    fam_syms = collections.defaultdict(collections.Counter)
    buckets = collections.Counter()
    subj = {}
    for s in samples:
        seen = set()
        for key, sym in s["named"].items():
            fam, kind = classify_symbol(sym)
            fam_ts[(fam, kind)] += 1
            fam_syms[(fam, kind)][sym] += 1
            seen.add((fam, kind))
            d = subj.setdefault(key, {"dwell": 0, "syms": collections.Counter()})
            d["dwell"] += 1
            d["syms"][sym] += 1
        for f in seen:
            fam_presence[f] += 1
        buckets.update(s["buckets"])

    total_ts = sum(buckets.values())
    families = []
    for (fam, kind), c in fam_ts.items():
        families.append({"family": fam, "kind": kind, "thread_samples": c,
                         "occupancy": c / n, "presence_pct": 100.0 * fam_presence[(fam, kind)] / n,
                         "top_symbols": [{"symbol": k, "n": v}
                                         for k, v in fam_syms[(fam, kind)].most_common(4)]})
    families.sort(key=lambda f: (KIND_ORDER.get(f["kind"], 9), -f["thread_samples"]))

    subjects = []
    for (pid, tid), d in subj.items():
        sym = d["syms"].most_common(1)[0][0]
        fam, kind = classify_symbol(sym)
        subjects.append({"pid": pid, "tid": tid, "comm": names.get((pid, tid), "?"),
                         "symbol": sym, "family": fam, "kind": kind,
                         "dwell_samples": d["dwell"], "dwell_pct": 100.0 * d["dwell"] / n,
                         "symbols": [{"symbol": k, "n": v} for k, v in d["syms"].most_common(3)]})
    # Ordered by MECHANISM CLASS first, then by dwell. This is NOT a severity ranking and dwell
    # is NOT a scale: an idle daemon parked in ep_poll dwells 100% of every window (the same
    # inversion `a-wait-fraction-cannot-separate-idle-from-saturated` names on the rq-wait axis),
    # which is exactly why the resource-kind rows are listed first and the idle ones are not
    # allowed to outrank them by being idle harder.
    subjects.sort(key=lambda r: (KIND_ORDER.get(r["kind"], 9), -r["dwell_samples"], r["pid"]))

    return {"n": n, "families": families, "subjects": subjects, "buckets": buckets,
            "total_thread_samples": total_ts,
            "masked_pct": (100.0 * buckets["masked"] / total_ts) if total_ts else None,
            "named_pct": (100.0 * buckets["named"] / total_ts) if total_ts else None}


def dominant_resource(agg):
    """The mechanism token a quantity arm cites, or None. Resource-kind only: handing mesh-psi
    `futex` (ambiguous) or `poll` (idle) as "the mechanism" would be worse than handing it
    nothing, because it reads as an answer."""
    for f in agg["families"]:
        if f["kind"] == "resource":
            return f
    return None


def cmdline_of(proot, pid):
    c = _read(os.path.join(proot, pid, "cmdline")) or ""
    return " ".join(c.replace("\0", " ").split())[:60]


# ─────────────────────────────── rendering ───────────────────────────────

def render(agg, meta, proot, topn):
    dom = dominant_resource(agg)
    if dom:
        head = "mechanism=%s(%s) %.2f thr/sample, seen in %.0f%% of samples" % (
            dom["family"], dom["top_symbols"][0]["symbol"], dom["occupancy"], dom["presence_pct"])
    else:
        head = "mechanism=none-resource-kind (no thread caught waiting on a kernel resource)"

    by_kind = collections.OrderedDict()
    for f in agg["families"]:
        by_kind.setdefault(f["kind"], []).append("%s %.2f" % (f["family"], f["occupancy"]))
    fam_txt = " | ".join("%s: %s" % (k, ", ".join(v)) for k, v in by_kind.items()) or "none named"

    # EVERY unknown-kind family is named with its symbols, not just the biggest one — the point
    # of the bucket is that a rotted rule shows up as a symbol nobody recognises, and a rendering
    # that printed only the top one would hide the new arrival behind the chronic helper.
    unk_txt = ""
    for f in [x for x in agg["families"] if x["kind"] == "unknown"]:
        syms = ",".join("%sx%d" % (s["symbol"], s["n"]) for s in f["top_symbols"])
        unk_txt += " | unclassified/%s %d thread-samples (%s)" % (
            f["family"], f["thread_samples"], syms)

    b = agg["buckets"]
    vis = ("named=%d masked=%d (%s) running=%d zombie=%d na=%d gone=%d" % (
        b["named"], b["masked"],
        "na" if agg["masked_pct"] is None else "%.1f%%" % agg["masked_pct"],
        b["running"], b["zombie"], b["na"], b["gone"]))

    line = ("[wchan] %s | %s%s | visibility %s | %d samples over %.1fs @%.2fHz, sweep %.0f/%.0fms "
            "mean/max = %.1f%% of the %.0fs cadence sampled | severity is not this sense's arm "
            "(mesh-psi io); the culprit is root-owned and structurally masked" % (
                head, fam_txt, unk_txt, vis, agg["n"], meta["window_s"], meta["hz_actual"],
                meta["scan_mean_ms"], meta["scan_max_ms"],
                100.0 * meta["window_s"] / CADENCE_S if CADENCE_S > 0 else 0.0, CADENCE_S))
    rows = []
    for r in agg["subjects"][:max(topn, 1)]:
        rows.append("  %-10s %-18s %5.1f%% dwell (%d/%d)  %s/%s %s %s" % (
            r["kind"], r["family"], r["dwell_pct"], r["dwell_samples"], agg["n"],
            r["pid"], r["tid"], r["comm"], cmdline_of(proot, r["pid"])))
    return line, rows


# ─────────────────────────────── self-test ───────────────────────────────

def _plant(root, spec):
    """Fixture /proc. spec: {pid: (cmdline, {tid: (wchan, statline_or_None)})}.
    statline is the RAW /proc/<tid>/stat text so the comm-with-paren trap is plantable."""
    for pid, (cmdline, tids) in spec.items():
        os.makedirs(os.path.join(root, pid), exist_ok=True)
        with open(os.path.join(root, pid, "cmdline"), "w") as fh:
            fh.write(cmdline.replace(" ", "\0"))
        for tid, (w, st) in tids.items():
            td = os.path.join(root, pid, "task", tid)
            os.makedirs(td, exist_ok=True)
            with open(os.path.join(td, "wchan"), "w") as fh:
                fh.write(w + "\n")
            with open(os.path.join(td, "comm"), "w") as fh:
                fh.write("t%s\n" % tid)
            if st is not None:
                with open(os.path.join(td, "stat"), "w") as fh:
                    fh.write(st + "\n")


def _selftest():
    import shutil
    import tempfile
    fails = []
    # Mutant children run the FIXTURE legs only: every mutant in the table below is targeted by a
    # fixture leg, and the live legs cost seconds that would push the parent past mesh-autowire's
    # `timeout 30`. The base run does exercise them — this flag never skips a leg a mutant needs.
    child = os.environ.get("MESH_WCHAN_MUTANT") == "1"

    def _t(cond, label):
        if cond:
            print("  ok: " + label)
        else:
            print("  FAIL: " + label)
            fails.append(label)

    d = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix="wchan-test-")
    try:
        # ── fixture: discover's measured futex case + the mask + the paren-comm trap ────────
        # 4242 is a python process whose LEADER sleeps in hrtimer_nanosleep while the actually
        # blocked non-leader tid sits in futex_wait_queue. This is what makes the pid-walk a
        # confident WRONG mechanism rather than a gap, so it is the pid-walk mutant's leg.
        # 1 is a root-owned sleeping task reading `0` — the permission mask, the zero mutant's leg.
        # 777's comm holds a space AND a paren (tmux), so whitespace field 3 yields state
        # `client)` — the state mutant's leg.
        f = os.path.join(d, "proc")
        _plant(f, {
            "4242": ("python3 -c ...", {"4242": ("hrtimer_nanosleep", None),
                                        "4243": ("futex_wait_queue", None)}),
            "1": ("/sbin/init", {"1": ("0", "1 (systemd) S 0 1 1 0 -1 4194560 1 2 3 4")}),
            "99": ("spin", {"99": ("0", "99 (spinner) R 0 99 99 0 -1 4194304 1 2 3 4")}),
            "98": ("gone", {"98": ("0", "98 (defunct) Z 0 98 98 0 -1 4194304 1 2 3 4")}),
            "777": ("tmux client", {"777": ("0", "777 (tmux: client) S 1 777 777 0 -1 4194304 1 2")}),
            "555": ("dd", {"555": ("blk_io_schedule", None)}),
            "556": ("future", {"556": ("zz_symbol_from_a_later_kernel", None)}),
        })
        names = {}
        samples = poll(f, plan_samples(1.0, 4.0), 100.0, set(), names, sleeper=lambda _s: None)
        agg = aggregate(samples, names)

        # 1. per-thread walk — the blocked NON-LEADER tid is the futex subject
        futex = [r for r in agg["subjects"] if r["family"] == "futex"]
        _t(len(futex) == 1 and futex[0]["tid"] == "4243" and futex[0]["pid"] == "4242",
           "the futex-blocked non-leader thread 4242/4243 is the subject (per-thread walk)")
        leader = [r for r in agg["subjects"] if r["tid"] == "4242"]
        _t(leader and leader[0]["symbol"] == "hrtimer_nanosleep" and leader[0]["kind"] == "idle",
           "...and its LEADER's hrtimer_nanosleep is reported separately, as the idle wait it is")

        # 2. `0` is never "not blocked" — three facts, three renderings
        _t(agg["buckets"]["masked"] == 2 * agg["n"] and agg["buckets"]["running"] == agg["n"],
           "a root-owned sleeping task reading 0 renders masked, never a not-blocked calm")
        _t(agg["buckets"]["zombie"] == agg["n"],
           "a zombie reading 0 renders zombie, not a calm")
        _t(resolve_zero("R") == "running" and resolve_zero("Z") == "zombie"
           and resolve_zero("D") == "masked" and resolve_zero(None) == "na",
           "resolve_zero: running / zombie / masked / na — every branch a claim about the task")
        _t(agg["masked_pct"] is not None and 24.9 < agg["masked_pct"] < 25.1,   # 2 of 8 threads
           "the masked share is published with the reading (%.1f%%) — the blindness is a number"
           % agg["masked_pct"])

        # 3. state parsed after the LAST ')' — the tmux comm with a space and a paren
        _t(parse_stat("777 (tmux: client) S 1 777") == ("S", "tmux: client"),
           "state parsed after the last ')' for a comm holding a space and a paren (masked, not na)")
        _t(parse_stat("1 (systemd) S 0 1")[0] == "S" and parse_stat("x")[0] is None,
           "...and an ordinary comm still parses, a malformed line renders None")

        # 4. the poll is a distribution, and one read is refused
        _t(agg["n"] >= 2 and plan_samples(1.0, 4.0) == 4 and plan_samples(0.0, 0.0) == 2,
           "sample_count %d >= 2 — plan_samples floors at 2, so a snapshot cannot be published"
           % agg["n"])
        _t(distribution_gate(1) is not None and distribution_gate(2) is None,
           "the sample_count gate refuses a single-sample reading and passes a real poll")

        # 5. prefix families + an explicit unknown bucket that is never absorbed
        _t(classify_symbol("blk_io_schedule") == ("io", "resource")
           and classify_symbol("rq_qos_wait") == ("io-throttle", "resource")
           and classify_symbol("folio_wait_bit_common") == ("wait-bit", "resource"),
           "prefix families: blk_io_schedule/rq_qos_wait/folio_wait_bit_common → resource kinds")
        _t(classify_symbol("do_poll.constprop.0") == ("poll", "idle"),
           "a compiler-suffixed symbol (measured live here) classifies — an exact table would miss it")
        _t(classify_symbol("futex_wait_queue") == ("futex", "ambiguous"),
           "futex is AMBIGUOUS, not contention — 972/1356 named threads sat there on an idle node")
        _t(classify_symbol("zz_symbol_from_a_later_kernel") == ("unknown", "unknown"),
           "an unmatched symbol lands in the unknown bucket, never absorbed into a neighbour")
        unk = [x for x in agg["families"] if x["kind"] == "unknown"]
        _t(unk and unk[0]["top_symbols"][0]["symbol"] == "zz_symbol_from_a_later_kernel",
           "...and the unknown bucket is REPORTED with its symbols, so table rot is visible")

        # 6. mechanism only — no severity anywhere in the reading
        dom = dominant_resource(agg)
        _t(dom is not None and dom["family"] == "io",
           "the dominant RESOURCE mechanism is io — the token a quantity arm cites")
        _t(dominant_resource({"families": [{"family": "futex", "kind": "ambiguous"},
                                           {"family": "poll", "kind": "idle"}]}) is None,
           "...and an ambiguous/idle-only window yields NO mechanism token, never a plausible one")
        line, _rows = render(agg, {"window_s": 1.0, "hz_actual": 4.0,
                                   "scan_mean_ms": 1.0, "scan_max_ms": 2.0}, f, 8)
        _t("severity is not this sense's arm" in line and "samples over" in line,
           "the reading states its window/sample count and disclaims severity in the line itself")

        if child:
            print("  (live + e2e legs skipped — this IS a mutant child; base run covers them)")
        else:
            # ── 7. LIVE control: the mask is real on THIS node, at this instant ────────────
            sp = subprocess.Popen(["sleep", "30"])
            time.sleep(0.25)
            ours = (_read("/proc/%d/wchan" % sp.pid) or "").strip()
            init = (_read("/proc/1/wchan") or "").strip()
            init_state = parse_stat(_read("/proc/1/stat") or "")[0]
            _t(ours and ours != "0",
               "live control: our own sleeper reads a symbol (%s)" % ours)
            _t(init == "0" and resolve_zero(init_state) == "masked",
               "live control: root pid 1 reads 0 at the same instant and renders masked (state %s)"
               % init_state)

            # ── 8. LIVE fixture PAIR: two processes, two DIFFERENT families ────────────────
            # A sense that returned a constant would pass every leg above. These two cannot both
            # be satisfied by one answer: a fifo reader and an O_DIRECT writer block on different
            # kernel resources, and the reading must say so.
            fifo = os.path.join(d, "fifo")
            os.mkfifo(fifo)
            ddout = os.path.join(d, "ddout")
            cat = subprocess.Popen(["cat", fifo])
            # bs=512 rather than 4k: the writer is IOPS-bound either way, so the small block
            # buys ~2s of life and a ~50% chance of being caught in D per read (measured here)
            # for 30MB of NVMe wear instead of 80MB — this runs hourly under mesh-doctor.
            dd = subprocess.Popen(["dd", "if=/dev/zero", "of=" + ddout, "bs=512", "count=60000",
                                   "oflag=direct", "status=none"])
            try:
                nm2 = {}
                # budget=1.0 disables the self-throttle for this leg ONLY. The live tool's
                # throttle stretches the period to ~10x the sweep, which would outlive the
                # fixture; the leg is about what the sense REPORTS, not about its pacing.
                sm2 = poll("/proc", 10, 20.0, {str(os.getpid())}, nm2, budget=1.0)
                ag2 = aggregate(sm2, nm2)
                got = {}
                for r in ag2["subjects"]:
                    if r["pid"] in (str(cat.pid), str(dd.pid)):
                        got[r["pid"]] = (r["family"], r["symbol"])
                fc = got.get(str(cat.pid))
                fd = got.get(str(dd.pid))
                _t(fc is not None and fd is not None,
                   "live pair: both the fifo reader and the O_DIRECT writer were caught blocked")
                _t(fc and fd and fc[0] != fd[0],
                   "live pair: two DIFFERENT families (%s vs %s) — the sense cannot pass by "
                   "returning a constant" % (fc and fc[1], fd and fd[1]))
                _t(fd is not None and classify_symbol(fd[1])[1] == "resource",
                   "live pair: the O_DIRECT writer classifies as a RESOURCE wait (%s)"
                   % (fd and fd[1]))
                _t(ag2["buckets"]["named"] > 0 and ag2["buckets"]["masked"] > 0,
                   "live read: %d named and %d masked thread-samples — both arms live"
                   % (ag2["buckets"]["named"], ag2["buckets"]["masked"]))
                mean_ms = sum(s["scan_ms"] for s in sm2) / len(sm2)
                _t(0 < mean_ms < 5000,
                   "live read: sweep cost %.0fms published with the reading (re-derived, not "
                   "inherited)" % mean_ms)
                _t(not [r for r in ag2["subjects"] if r["pid"] == str(os.getpid())],
                   "live read: the probe's OWN pid is excluded — it cannot measure itself")
            finally:
                for p in (cat, dd, sp):
                    try:
                        p.kill()
                        p.wait(timeout=5)
                    except Exception:
                        pass

            # ── 9. e2e, and the log is written ONCE at the END, never per sample ───────────
            elog = os.path.join(d, "e2e.log")
            env = dict(os.environ, MESH_WCHAN_WINDOW_S="2.0", MESH_WCHAN_HZ="4",
                       MESH_WCHAN_LOG=elog)          # never the live artifact
            p = subprocess.Popen([sys.executable, os.path.abspath(__file__), "--json", "--log"],
                                 stdout=subprocess.PIPE, stderr=subprocess.PIPE, text=True, env=env)
            grew_early = False
            while p.poll() is None:
                if os.path.exists(elog) and os.path.getsize(elog) > 0:
                    grew_early = True
                    break
                time.sleep(0.1)
            out, err = p.communicate(timeout=60)
            _t(not grew_early,
               "the log stayed EMPTY for the whole poll — buffered in memory, written once at the end")
            try:
                j = json.loads(out)
            except ValueError:
                j = None
            _t(j is not None and p.returncode == 0, "e2e --json reading parses (rc=%d) %s"
               % (p.returncode, err.strip()[:80]))
            if j:
                _t(j["sample_count"] >= 2 and j["window_s"] > 0 and j["hz_actual"] > 0,
                   "e2e: sample_count=%d over %.1fs @%.2fHz published with the reading"
                   % (j["sample_count"], j["window_s"], j["hz_actual"]))
                _t("level" not in j and "severity" not in j and "score" not in j,
                   "e2e: the reading carries NO level/severity/score — mechanism only (trap 7)")
                _t(j["visibility"]["masked"] > 0 and j["visibility"]["named"] > 0,
                   "e2e: %d named / %d masked thread-samples — the mask is reported, not hidden"
                   % (j["visibility"]["named"], j["visibility"]["masked"]))
                _t(j["self_excluded"] and j["cadence_s"] > 0
                   and 0 < j["wallclock_sampled_pct"] < 100,
                   "e2e: window/cadence coverage %.1f%% published — the sample never reads as the "
                   "interval" % j["wallclock_sampled_pct"])
            lines = (_read(elog) or "").splitlines()
            _t(len(lines) == 1,
               "the log gained EXACTLY ONE line for the whole poll (%d)" % len(lines))

        # ── 10. MUTANTS, each from a scratch copy, each red on ITS OWN leg ────────────────
        if os.environ.get("MESH_WCHAN_NO_MUTANTS") == "1":
            print("  (mutant pass skipped — this IS a mutant)")
        else:
            src = _read(os.path.abspath(__file__))
            M = "# MUT" + "ANT:"          # assembled so the table never matches itself
            mutants = [
                ('        return sorted(os.listdir(os.path.join(proot, pid, "task")))   ' + M + "walk",
                 "        return [pid]   # mutated",
                 "per-thread walk", "walk /proc/<pid> instead of task/<tid>"),
                ('    return "masked"   ' + M + "zero",
                 '    return "not_blocked"   # mutated',
                 "never a not-blocked calm", "render a masked 0 as not-blocked"),
                ("    return max(2, int(round(window_s * hz)))   " + M + "samples",
                 "    return 1   # mutated",
                 "sample_count", "sample once instead of polling"),
                ('    i = s.rfind(")")   ' + M + "state\n"
                 "    if i < 0:\n"
                 "        return None, None\n"
                 "    tail = s[i + 1:].split()\n"
                 '    return (tail[0] if tail else None), s[s.find("(") + 1:i]',
                 "    f = s.split()   # mutated\n"
                 "    return (f[2] if len(f) > 2 else None), (f[1] if len(f) > 1 else None)",
                 "last ')'", "parse the state as whitespace field 3"),
                ('    return "unknown", "unknown"   ' + M + "unknown",
                 '    return "io", "resource"   # mutated',
                 "unknown bucket", "absorb an unmatched symbol into a neighbouring family"),
            ]
            env = dict(os.environ, MESH_WCHAN_NO_MUTANTS="1", MESH_WCHAN_MUTANT="1")
            for i, (old, new, expect, what) in enumerate(mutants):
                if src.count(old) != 1:
                    _t(False, "mutant %d (%s) has no unique target — the mutant is VACUOUS" % (i, what))
                    continue
                mp = os.path.join(d, "mutant%d" % i)
                with open(mp, "w", encoding="utf-8") as fh:
                    fh.write(src.replace(old, new))
                os.chmod(mp, 0o755)
                r = subprocess.run([sys.executable, mp, "--test"], capture_output=True,
                                   text=True, timeout=120, env=env)
                out = r.stdout + r.stderr
                # A non-zero exit proves nothing on its own — a mutant can go red for the wrong
                # reason. Require the FAIL line that belongs to THIS mutation.
                red_here = any(ln.lstrip().startswith("FAIL:") and expect in ln
                               for ln in out.splitlines())
                _t(r.returncode != 0 and red_here,
                   "mutant: %s → RED on its own leg (rc=%d)" % (what, r.returncode))

        if fails:
            print("smoke-test: FAIL (%d: %s)" % (len(fails), "; ".join(fails[:3])))
            return 1
        print("smoke-test: ok (per-thread walk + 0→running/masked/zombie/na + last-')' state + "
              "poll floor & gate + prefix families with a reported unknown bucket + no severity"
              + ("" if child else " + live mask control + fifo/dd two-family pair + "
                                 "write-once-at-the-end")
              + " + 5 mutants each red on its own leg)")
        return 0
    finally:
        shutil.rmtree(d, ignore_errors=True)


# ─────────────────────────────── main ───────────────────────────────

def _argval(argv, flag, cast, default):
    if flag in argv:
        try:
            return cast(argv[argv.index(flag) + 1])
        except (IndexError, ValueError):
            pass
    return default


def main(argv):
    if "--test" in argv:
        return _selftest()

    topn = _argval(argv, "--top", int, TOPN_DEFAULT)
    window_s = _argval(argv, "--window", float, WINDOW_S)
    hz = _argval(argv, "--hz", float, HZ)

    names = {}
    exclude = {str(os.getpid())}          # trap 4: the probe is not a subject of its own reading
    t0 = time.time()
    samples = poll(PROC, plan_samples(window_s, hz), hz, exclude, names)
    elapsed = time.time() - t0

    if not samples:
        print("mesh-wchan: n/a — no readable %s/<pid>/task/<tid>/wchan" % PROC, file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    reason = distribution_gate(len(samples))
    if reason:
        print("mesh-wchan: n/a — %s" % reason, file=sys.stderr)
        return 2

    agg = aggregate(samples, names)
    if agg["total_thread_samples"] == 0:
        print("mesh-wchan: n/a — not one thread was readable in %d sweeps" % len(samples),
              file=sys.stderr)
        return 2

    scans = [s["scan_ms"] for s in samples]
    meta = {"window_s": elapsed, "hz_actual": (len(samples) / elapsed) if elapsed > 0 else 0.0,
            "scan_mean_ms": sum(scans) / len(scans), "scan_max_ms": max(scans)}
    dom = dominant_resource(agg)

    if "--mech" in argv:
        # The token a quantity arm cites. `none` is a real answer: nothing was caught waiting on
        # a kernel resource in this window. It is NOT a claim that the node is calm — that
        # quantity is mesh-psi's, and the masked share below says how blind this reading was.
        print("%s %s %.2f masked=%s samples=%d window=%.1fs" % (
            dom["family"] if dom else "none",
            dom["top_symbols"][0]["symbol"] if dom else "-",
            dom["occupancy"] if dom else 0.0,
            "na" if agg["masked_pct"] is None else "%.1f%%" % agg["masked_pct"],
            agg["n"], meta["window_s"]))
        return 0

    line, rows = render(agg, meta, PROC, topn)

    if "--log" in argv:
        # ONE write, at the END, and BEFORE the output branch — a `--log` that lived only on the
        # text path would silently drop the reflex's whole artifact the day someone added --json
        # to its reflex-args, and the log would go quiet without anything going red.
        # Buffering the samples until here is the reason this reading is not measuring itself
        # (trap 4): an append per sweep catches the probe's own shell in the block-layer throttle.
        try:
            os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(LOG), exist_ok=True)
            with open(LOG, "a", encoding="utf-8") as fh:
                fh.write("%s %s\n" % (time.strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ", time.gmtime()), line))
            old = _read(LOG)
            if old is not None:
                ls = old.splitlines(True)
                if len(ls) > LOG_KEEP * 2:      # prune rarely, in bulk
                    with open(LOG, "w", encoding="utf-8") as fh:
                        fh.writelines(ls[-LOG_KEEP:])
        except OSError:
            pass

    if "--json" in argv:
        b = agg["buckets"]
        print(json.dumps({
            "mechanism": None if not dom else {
                "family": dom["family"], "symbol": dom["top_symbols"][0]["symbol"],
                "occupancy": round(dom["occupancy"], 3),
                "presence_pct": round(dom["presence_pct"], 1)},
            "families": [dict(f, occupancy=round(f["occupancy"], 3),
                              presence_pct=round(f["presence_pct"], 1)) for f in agg["families"]],
            "subjects": [dict(r, dwell_pct=round(r["dwell_pct"], 1),
                              cmd=cmdline_of(PROC, r["pid"]))
                         for r in agg["subjects"][:max(topn, 1)]],
            "visibility": {"named": b["named"], "masked": b["masked"], "running": b["running"],
                           "zombie": b["zombie"], "na": b["na"], "gone": b["gone"],
                           "masked_pct": None if agg["masked_pct"] is None
                                         else round(agg["masked_pct"], 1),
                           "note": "masked = root-owned and unreadable; the writeback/journal/"
                                   "reclaim threads that CAUSE an io stall are all in here"},
            "sample_count": agg["n"], "window_s": round(meta["window_s"], 2),
            "hz_actual": round(meta["hz_actual"], 2), "hz_target": hz,
            "scan_ms_mean": round(meta["scan_mean_ms"], 1),
            "scan_ms_max": round(meta["scan_max_ms"], 1),
            "cadence_s": CADENCE_S,
            "wallclock_sampled_pct": round(100.0 * meta["window_s"] / CADENCE_S, 2)
                                     if CADENCE_S > 0 else None,
            "self_excluded": sorted(exclude),
            # There is deliberately no `level`/`severity`/`score` key here, and the e2e leg
            # asserts their ABSENCE — a consumer must not be able to read a harm scale off this.
            "no_severity": "mechanism only — a count of wchan sightings is not a quantity of "
                           "harm; PSI-io remains the severity arm",
            "ts": time.strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ", time.gmtime()),
        }))
        return 0

    print(line)
    for r in rows:
        print(r)
    return 0


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main(sys.argv[1:]))
